+No P0 findings. The Metadata approach is sound; the glossary plan needs two substantive corrections.
+
+- **P1 — “Current list → appends” is false.** [Plan:39](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/docs/plans/261003c-glossary-find-more-at-the-top-and-metadata-press-closes.md:39) distinguishes only prompt versions. [`existingFor`:415](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/glossary.ts:415) also requires matching source and profile hashes. `owner.more(owner.profiled)` preserves whether a profile is used, but the server resolves **today’s** profile ([routes.ts:9967](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/routes.ts:9967)). Changing—or clearing—a previously used profile therefore makes “Find more” replace the list. Source changes do likewise. Checking `profileChanged` alone misses clearing: [`profileIsStale`:275](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/profile.ts:275) returns false when the current profile is absent. Base the label on the actual append/rewrite decision; [`glossaryRunKind`:455](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/glossary.ts:455) already centralises it, provided it receives this button’s effective profile.
+
+- **P1 — The preservation promise overstates what remains accessible.** [Plan:29](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/docs/plans/261003c-glossary-find-more-at-the-top-and-metadata-press-closes.md:29) and its tooltip promise need qualification. IDs are inherited only when the source hash matches ([glossary.ts:1436](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/glossary.ts:1436)), and only for matching names/aliases. If a model-found term disappears, its lookup and hide rows remain stored, but no entry attaches them; its `?term=` link loses its target ([pg.ts:3525](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/store/pg.ts:3525)). Added terms survive separately, although a model entry can absorb their displayed row, and **their hide does not follow** ([pg.ts:3515](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/store/pg.ts:3515)). “Find terms again” honestly names an outdated-list rewrite, but the tooltip should explicitly say some existing terms may disappear.
+
+- **P2 — Moving the footer leaves a second run control on stale-source lists.** [GlossaryPanel.tsx:504](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/web/GlossaryPanel.tsx:504) already draws “Find them again”, progress and Cancel in the stale banner. Merely moving `Foot` leaves duplicate controls and progress, contradicting “one button in one place”. Keep the stale explanation, but let the top row own the run controls.
+
+- **P2 — ID inheritance did not arrive after 260929c.** [Plan:28](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/docs/plans/261003c-glossary-find-more-at-the-top-and-metadata-press-closes.md:28) is historically false: 260929c’s commit `f46e2dc7` already contains `idsByTerm` and the same-source inheritance guard. The recent additions are hiding and reader-added terms.
+
+- **P2 — An existing encoded-parameter exception undermines the drawer-stripping claim.** [`carriedSearch`:624](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/web/router.ts:624) strips literal `panel=`, but retains `%70anel=questions`. Query parsing decodes that key, so returning can reopen the drawer. This predates the toggle; decode keys when filtering if the plan promises drawers always close.
+
+Ordinary Metadata navigation preserves `mode`, `margin`, `at` and sub-mode parameters such as `summary=simple` or `remember=quiz`: the helper carries everything except literal `panel=`. The visitor metadata page mounts the same Dock ([PublicPages.tsx:298](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb-glossary-findmore-metadata-toggle/src/web/PublicPages.tsx:298)); no owner callback is needed. Position restoration is to the saved block, not an exact pixel offset.
+
+Visitors, zero-entry lists and running jobs are otherwise handled by the proposed existing guards. Preserve `job || starting`, the ready-status guard, and failure rendering. Add coverage for those states and the Metadata return chord.
+
+The simplest implementation remains hoisting the existing run UI and changing one shared Metadata destination for both link and chord. No `modePress` extension or new navigation state is needed.
+
+`glossary/7` is confirmed in code. The production `/4` stamp and “probably most of the shelf” cannot be verified from code alone. I changed no files.
\ No newline at end of file
